      "body": "preprocess_video picked frames with np.linspace(..., dtype=np.int64), which truncates. qwen-vl-utils rounds to the nearest frame. Round with np.rint and keep the np.unique dedup from #12240. Frame count, token count and speed are unchanged.\n\n<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\n\n<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title.\nType: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, or Chore.\nScope: any module or model name (no fixed list or letter-case restriction), e.g. attention, qwen3, or flash-attn.\nHardware: optional single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend.\nTitle: no letter-case restriction.\nReverts: use GitHub's default title, Revert \"original title\".\nExamples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance. -->\n\n## Motivation\n\n`preprocess_video` picks frame indices with `np.linspace(..., dtype=np.int64)`, which truncates, while qwen-vl-utils rounds to the nearest frame. The rounding was dropped in #12240 to avoid duplicates, but since `nframes <= total_frames`, rounding can't produce duplicates.\n\nExample, 8 frames from a 200-frame video:\n- before: `0, 28, 56, 85, 113, 142, 170, 199`\n- after (= qwen-vl-utils): `0, 28, 57, 85, 114, 142, 171, 199`\n\n**You may already be aware of this; if the truncation is intentional, please feel free to close this PR.**\n\n## Modifications\n\nRound with `np.rint` before casting to int64, and keep `np.unique`. Frame count and token count are unchanged. \n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo impact: only the index computation changes\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41217408340](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41217408340)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41217408377](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41217408377)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41217408342](https://git